From: surface-kit
Subject: [PATCH] software_isp: Colour sums scale, highlight shoulder, lens shading

- SwStatsCpu: keep the colour sums on the 8-bit scale of the black level.
  Unpacked 10/12-bit lines summed raw samples while AWB subtracted the
  8-bit black level from them, leaving a light dependent colour cast.
- Highlight shoulder instead of a hard clip after the colour gains (GPU
  shaders and CPU lookup tables), and in the GPU path pixels where the
  sensor saturated are blended towards neutral, so whites keep gradation
  and clipped whites don't turn pink or green.
- Radial lens shading correction (GPU debayer): 1 + k1 r^2 + k2 r^4 per raw
  channel, r over half the image width, from a new Lsc tuning algorithm.
- Surface Pro 7 tuning: the drivers set black level 16 (10-bit), not 64;
  ov8865 shading fitted on a flat field (corners ~3x darker).

---
--- c/include/libcamera/internal/software_isp/debayer_params.h	2026-01-29 13:17:26.000000000 +0100
+++ b/include/libcamera/internal/software_isp/debayer_params.h	2026-10-06 22:54:59.691752662 +0200
@@ -23,6 +23,13 @@
 	float gamma;
 	float contrastExp;
 	RGB<float> gains;
+	/*
+	 * Radial lens shading gain per raw channel, 1 + k1 r^2 + k2 r^4, with r
+	 * the distance from the image centre over half the image width. Only
+	 * the GPU debayer applies it.
+	 */
+	RGB<float> lscK1;
+	RGB<float> lscK2;
 };
 
 } /* namespace libcamera */
